From c05f743abadd9bc95ca627476cd354d9efb30f44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maxime <maxime.lefrancois@emse.fr>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 01:55:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Support rml:childMap and rml:parentMap in join conditions
 (RML-Core)

RML-Core allows the two sides of a join condition to be expression maps,
rml:childMap and rml:parentMap (a reference, a template or a constant), in
place of rml:child and rml:parent. The mapping stopped with "One of the join
conditions ... is missing rr:parent" (RMLTC0030a-f, kg-construct/rml-core).

MappingFactory now builds the executor of such a map with
RecordFunctionExecutorFactory, and compares the string values of the two
sides (a constant "100" and a JSON number 100 are equal).
Tests: RMLTC0030a-f of MapperNewRMLCoreJSONTest, copied from the CG suite.
